Now I understand the vulnerability. Let me analyze `lex_multiline_string`:

```c
static void *lex_multiline_string(struct lexer *lexer)
{
    char *end = (peek(lexer) == '"') ? "\"\"\"" : "'''";

    advance_n(lexer, strlen("'''") - 1);  // advances 2 chars

    do {
        if (!strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)) {
            emit(lexer, LEXEME_STRING);
            lexer->pos += 3;
            return lex_config;
        }
    } while (next(lexer) != '\0');

    return lex_error(lexer, "EOF while scanning multiline string");
}
```

The issue: `strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)` reads 3 bytes from `lexer->pos`. If the input ends right after the opening `'''` or `"""` (i.e., there are fewer than 3 bytes remaining), `strncmp` will read past the end of the buffer — a global-buffer-overflow READ of 3 bytes.

